WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.270
Have you ever tasted a snack that is crunchy,
spicy, tangy and refreshing all at once?

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:50.149
Meet Jhal Muri, one of Bengal's most iconic
street foods.

00:01:31.198 --> 00:01:38.018
Originating in Kolkata, West Bengal, this humble
snack has roots in Bengal's traditional food culture.

00:02:16.796 --> 00:02:28.156
It became especially popular as a street food
during World War II, when migrant workers from
Bihar helped bring it to the streets of Kolkata.

00:03:02.395 --> 00:03:14.395
The secret is in its simple yet flavourful ingredients:
crispy puffed rice, roasted peanuts, fresh onions,
tomatoes, cucumber, boiled potatoes, green chillies,
coriander, lemon juice and aromatic mustard oil,
mixed with traditional Indian spices and crunchy
savoury mixtures.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:59.994
It also offers nutritional goodness. Puffed rice
provides carbohydrates for energy, peanuts contribute
plant protein and healthy fats, while fresh vegetables
add fibre, vitamins and minerals.

00:04:33.593 --> 00:04:41.773
But why does everyone love Jhal Muri? Because it is
affordable, freshly prepared, light and full of flavour.

00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:24.641
Every bite brings together crunchiness, freshness,
spice and a wonderful tangy kick.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:15.240
Jhal Muri is more than just a snack. It is the true
taste of Kolkata's street-food culture, bringing
happiness in every crunchy bite.
